<editorial-block
  class="breakoutX"
  align="right"
  caption="The defibrillator home."
>
  <h3>Aims of WHCRG</h3>
  <p>As a resilience hub we will endeavour to:</p>
  <ol class="points-list">
    <li>
      To open the hall as a 'safe refuge' providing heat, light and phone
      charging facilities for West/mur community and anyone visiting.
    </li>
    <li>
      To maintain contact with the Angus Council Resilience Officer throughout
      any emergency.
    </li>
    <li>
      Use the hall as a receiving/distribution centre for equipment/supplies
      during an emergency.
    </li>
    <li>
      Provide a localised hub for use by the emergency services/utility
      companies in time of emergency.
    </li>
    <li>
      Address the wellbeing of those in the community who are most vulnerable.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <img
    slot="image"
    :src="$data.page.url + '/generator-1920.avif'"
    alt="Westmuir generator"
    width="1920"
    sizes="(min-width: 50rem) 35ch, 90vw"
  />
</editorial-block>

<h3>Opening the resilience hub</h3>

<p>
  WHCRG will try to open Westmuir Hall as a Resilience Hub under the following
  circumstances:
</p>
<ol class="points-list">
  <li>
    There is a specific request made to open the hub by Angus Council Resilience
    Team.
  </li>
  <li>
    There is a specific request to open the hub by one or more of the emergency
    services (police, fire, ambulance).
  </li>
  <li>
    There is a specific request to open the hub by one or more of the utility
    companies (gas, water, electricity).
  </li>
  <li>
    WHCRG committee become aware of a serious situation that will affect the
    community but there has been no specific request made by any of the above to
    open the Resilience Hub.
  </li>
</ol>
<p>
  When dealing with an incident or emergency WHCRG volunteers must not take
  unacceptable risks that place themselves or others in danger.
</p>
<p>
  Further advice and Information can be found online at
  <a href="https://www.readyscotland.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
    >www.readyscotland.org</a
  >
</p>

